      "rationale": "The report says the 'python' output format regressed so that the produced assignment string gets an unexpected leading \"\\n\". Reading sqlparse/filters/output.py shows OutputPythonFilter._process uses `if self.count >= 1:` to decide whether to emit a leading newline, while the equivalent (and correctly behaving) OutputPHPFilter uses `if self.count > 1:` \u2014 i.e. only statements after the first get a separating newline. The expected values in the tests (`sql = 'select * from foo;'` with no leading newline, and `sql2 = ...` on a new line for the second statement) reflect that intended, documented \"one assignment per statement\" behavior, matching the report's failing assertion.",
